WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.639
I want a clean graphic of the latest German
poll for an article. A warmer background, a

00:00:05.639 --> 00:00:09.260
clear headline, and a style I can use again.
Let's make it.

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:15.338
I'll search for latest polls. These previews
already show the data. This first layout is a

00:00:15.338 --> 00:00:16.487
good starting point.

00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:21.213
Now, Edit. I'll start with the headline.

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:26.773
Germany, the latest poll. Short enough to read
at a glance. There we go.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:33.300
Under Text and type, I'll switch to Subtitle
and add a little context. This is voting

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.540
intention, not an election result.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:40.735
I only want to change the headline here, so
I'll switch back to Title. Then Change

00:00:40.735 --> 00:00:45.107
typeface. I'll search for Georgia. There, that
feels more like an editorial graphic.

00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:52.463
Back to the title. A little bigger. Not too
much. Yes, that reads better.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.360
In Colours and background, I'll use a warm
off-white. The party colours stay as they are.

00:01:03.283 --> 00:01:08.428
That's the look. A design saves this particular
graphic. A style saves the visual choices, so I

00:01:08.428 --> 00:01:10.323
can reuse them with different data.

00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:16.593
I'll call this Germany, Editorial, and save the
design. Then I'll save its style as well.

00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:25.279
Next takes me through the type, colours, and
other visual settings. I'll keep the choices

00:01:25.279 --> 00:01:29.437
I've already made. And here's the name:
Editorial, Paper. Save style.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:37.853
Back to the preview, then All designs. I'll try
Newsroom this time. Now Apply a style. I'll

00:01:37.853 --> 00:01:40.727
choose Editorial, Paper, the one I just saved.

00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:49.877
Same typeface, same background. A different
layout, without doing all that again.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.433
Before I use it, a quick check in Info. Who
carried out the poll, when was it published,

00:01:55.433 --> 00:01:58.960
and what does it measure? That's the context I
need for my article.

00:02:00.283 --> 00:02:05.085
For this article, I want a fixed image. An
embed is the other option for a website. Check

00:02:05.085 --> 00:02:07.243
its update behaviour before you publish.

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:13.531
Download PNG opens the final preview. I'll
check the layout here, then download the image.

00:02:13.531 --> 00:02:13.830
Done.

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:19.273
And if I need it on a website instead, Embed
opens the code and its preview.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:25.234
There's my graphic, with the source still
attached. And next time, I can start with my

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:25.930
saved style.
